    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena measured her pencil as 12.45 cm and her pen as 12.5 cm.\n\"Which is longer?\" she asked."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "tenths",
     "hundredths",
     "round"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To compare decimals, compare the whole parts first, then tenths, hundredths and so on. 12.5 is 12.50, which is greater than 12.45.\nTo round a decimal to one place, look at the next digit. 12.45 rounds to 12.5 because 5 rounds up.\nAdding a zero at the end of a decimal does not change its value."
    }
